# The Sextile Tour: the keys that make docs/tour.svg.
#
# A key file is plain text. Each line is one of:
#
#   # a comment            a line that starts with #
#   @session NAME          the session the tour runs in (the unnamed one without it)
#   @start DURATION        how long the opening picture rests before the first key (default 1s)
#   KEY DURATION           press KEY, then rest DURATION on the picture it makes
#
# KEY is written as the Keybindings list writes it: <down>, <enter>, <esc>,
# <space>, <ctrl+o>, <alt+x>, or a bare character such as 0, / or u. The one
# character that is written in brackets is # (<#>), so it is not read as a comment.
# DURATION is Go's: 800ms, 1.5s, 2s.
#
# The tour starts with one chart, Sextile 0.1.0 (the first public release), beside Now,
# neither selected, in the session Sextile Tour. The picture is 132 columns by 40 rows
# with the clock fixed. Regenerate it after a change here:
#   go test ./internal/ui -run '^TestTourIsDrawn$' -demo
#
@session Sextile Tour
@start 2.5s

# The cursor goes from the chart to Now.
<down> 1500ms
# Enter goes into Details on the Timeline, ] shows the Moon, ] the report, Esc comes back.
<enter> 1500ms
] 2s
] 2s
<esc> 1500ms

# 3 goes to Bodies; Details shows the aspects of the planet under the cursor.
3 2s
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms
<down> 400ms

# 4 goes to Aspects; Details lists every aspect.
4 2500ms

# Enter goes into Details; / searches, and ura keeps the rows with Uranus.
<enter> 1500ms
/ 1s
u 600ms
r 600ms
a 2s
<enter> 1500ms
# Esc goes back to Aspects.
<esc> 3s
